    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d997">

                <pb facs="1342" n="1332" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1332"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50/1–345</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Appointed Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 53</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-03">January 3,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received January 24.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The appointed Ambassador has the honor to
                    transmit herewith a copy of an article regarding postwar policy toward economic
                    enterprises which appeared in the Government sponsored <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >National Herald</hi>, English language newspaper of Chungking, December 29,
                    1944.</p>
                <p>The article quotes a statement attributed to a spokesman of the Supreme National
                    Defense Council. When asked by a member of the Embassy for a copy of the policy
                    statement agreed upon by the Council, General Wu Te-chen, Secretary-General of
                    the Central Executive Committee of the Kuomintang, replied that it had appeared
                    in the press on December 29th. It is believed, therefore, that the press
                    statement was fully authorized.</p>
                <p>It may be remarked that the contents of the statement as published in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">National Herald</hi> conform closely to information
                    contained in previously transmitted memoranda of conversations between
                    Government and Party leaders, and members of the Embassy. It is consistent also
                    with the statements of Dr. Sun Fo<anchor n="2" xml:id="d997-f1"/> in a recent
                    address. A copy of his statement was enclosed with despatch no. 3212, on
                    December 8, 1944,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d997-f2"/> entitled “Address by Dr. Sun
                    Fo on China’s Postwar Economic Policy.”</p>


                <xi:include href="d997-a1.xml" xpointer="d997-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
